  "source_conclusion": "The complete overlay-detach fix is already present in the owned historical select. Untouched16 legacy and the current owned template bind detach to close(); both minimum public CDK overlay/scroll implementations carry native scrolling through the close strategy and OverlayRef detachment to that output. The stale earlier source-line proof remains retired. This is a completed source conclusion with mandatory artifact-required real-scroll behavior; no source record or synthetic fixture is a packed/native, G11 or security pass.",
  "hunk_reviews": [
    {
      "hunk": 1,
      "file": "src/material/select/select.html",
      "judgment": "The sole runtime addition binds the connected overlay detach output to close(). Untouched16 legacy already had this binding and the owned template retains it. Owned close guards actual-open state, restores key orientation and notifies touch once before its owned exit/detach path. Retaining the existing binding requires no product or consumer structure/style change."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 2,
      "file": "src/material/select/select.spec.ts",
      "judgment": "The added public CloseScrollStrategy and Overlay imports support the new scroll regression. They do not authorize introducing private CDK symbols or altering owned scroll-strategy token identity."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 3,
      "file": "src/material/select/select.spec.ts",
      "judgment": "Import reordering leaves symbols unchanged except the public MAT_SELECT_SCROLL_STRATEGY test override. The owned fixture uses its distinct MAT_LEGACY_SELECT_SCROLL_STRATEGY and the current companion uses its own current token in isolated scopes."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 4,
      "file": "src/material/select/select.spec.ts",
      "judgment": "The regression uses a close scroll strategy, emits a scroll dispatcher subject and asserts panelOpen false. The required packed case uses a real registered CdkScrollable native scroll event and real public close strategy/overlay/directive rather than the upstream fake dispatcher. Two cycles verify value/focus/ARIA, exact detach/output counts, idle scrolling, reopen and teardown. These actual component observations have not yet executed."
    }
  ],
